## PATCH 9: Prediction Monitoring

**Problem:** No visibility into what the model is doing in production.

- [ ] Log every API prediction: timestamp, input features, predicted class, confidence, response time
- [ ] Save logs to `data/logs/predictions.jsonl` (one JSON object per line)
- [ ] Add script: `scripts/monitor_drift.py` that reads logs and reports:
  - Prediction distribution over time (is one class dominating?)
  - Average confidence trending down?
  - Input feature distributions shifting?
- [ ] Add alerting thresholds (e.g. warn if >70% of predictions are the same class)

